{
  "_README": [
    "Reviewed mapping from shopper language to catalog values. EVERY value named here",
    "must exist in the catalog (see analysis/catalog_stats.json); scripts/check_lexicon.py",
    "fails the build if one does not. This file is data, not code: review it with a",
    "fashion eye and correct anything odd.",
    "",
    "synonyms: a word or phrase a shopper uses -> the catalog attributes it means.",
    "intents:  an occasion or need -> the catalog attributes that defensibly answer it.",
    "          Intents are weaker than synonyms and only nudge ranking.",
    "",
    "Intent entries are the only place where a query word that names no product maps to",
    "products at all, so they are the difference between answering 'something for a lazy",
    "Sunday' and abstaining on it."
  ],
